<article class="env-proposition" id="4273">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/4273">Proposition <span data-tag="4273">2.2.2.7</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a simplicial set. Then the map $p_ S: |S|_{Q^{\bullet }} \rightarrow S$ induced by $\pi $ is a weak homotopy equivalence. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Consider the collection $A$ of simplicial sets $S$ for which the assertion of Proposition <a href="/tag/4273" data-tag="4273">2.2.2.7</a> holds. Since $A$ is stable under filtered colimits, it will suffice to prove that every simplicial set $S$ having only finitely many nondegenerate simplices belongs to $A$. We prove this by induction on the dimension $n$ of $S$, and the number of nondegenerate simplices of $S$ of dimension $n$. If $S = \emptyset $, there is nothing to prove; otherwise we may write 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[ S \simeq S' \coprod _{ \bd \Delta ^ n } \Delta ^ n  \]
</div>
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  |S|_{Q^{\bullet }} \simeq |S'|_{Q^{\bullet }} \coprod _{ |\bd \Delta ^ n|_{Q^{\bullet }} } |\Delta ^ n|_{Q^{\bullet }}. \]
</div>
    <p>
       Since both of these pushouts are homotopy pushouts, it suffices to show that $p_{S'}$, $p_{\bd \Delta ^ n}$, and $p_{\Delta ^ n}$ are weak homotopy equivalences. For $p_{S'}$ and $p_{\bd \Delta ^ n}$, this follows from the inductive hypothesis; for $p_{\Delta ^ n}$, we need only observe that both $\Delta ^ n$ and $|\Delta ^ n|_{Q^{\bullet }} = Q^ n$ are weakly contractible. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>